WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:19.624
At school on Monday morning, Katie was mad, but she was also worried.

2
00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:25.744
If she didn't make up with Luke and Carlos, her square-dance plans were finished.

3
00:00:25.745 --> 00:00:29.057
She handed a note to Joy.

4
00:00:29.058 --> 00:00:32.682
"Please pass this to Carlos," she said.

5
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:34.754
She gave a note to Olivia.

6
00:00:34.755 --> 00:00:37.570
"Please pass this to Luke."

7
00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:39.742
The notes said the same thing:

8
00:00:39.743 --> 00:00:44.567
Come to dance practice tonight!

9
00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:50.032
N-O spells NO, wrote Carlos.

10
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:55.366
NO WAY, wrote Luke.

11
00:00:55.367 --> 00:01:01.094
"It's time for Laura's report on eyes," said Ms. Barrow.

12
00:01:01.095 --> 00:01:06.092
Laura carried a small pink suitcase to the front of the room.

13
00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:11.145
"Everyone, I'm worried about your eyes!" she said.

14
00:01:11.146 --> 00:01:13.062
"You must protect them!"

15
00:01:13.063 --> 00:01:16.630
Her eyes got big behind her glasses.

16
00:01:16.631 --> 00:01:20.890
"Watch out for sharp things—like scissors!"

17
00:01:20.891 --> 00:01:25.736
Joy remembered when Katie ran down the steps with scissors.

18
00:01:25.737 --> 00:01:30.189
She kicked Katie's desk to make sure she was listening.

19
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:35.766
Laura continued. "Watch out for flying things—like darts.

20
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:40.172
And exploding things—like firecrackers.

21
00:01:40.173 --> 00:01:43.896
And things that splash—like paint remover!"

22
00:01:43.897 --> 00:01:47.113
Laura reached inside her suitcase.

23
00:01:47.114 --> 00:01:50.878
"These are safety glasses," she said.

24
00:01:50.879 --> 00:01:53.724
"They fit over regular glasses.

25
00:01:53.725 --> 00:01:58.875
Wear them when you do science experiments or use tools."

26
00:01:58.876 --> 00:02:01.939
Laura pulled out more glasses.

27
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:08.074
"These are very cool sports glasses that I wear when I play softball.

28
00:02:08.075 --> 00:02:13.420
And these sunglasses protect my eyes from harmful sunrays.

29
00:02:13.421 --> 00:02:20.550
If you have trouble reading your books or seeing what Ms. Barrow writes on the board, tell your parents.

30
00:02:20.551 --> 00:02:22.731
Maybe you need glasses.

31
00:02:22.732 --> 00:02:25.315
I wear glasses all the time.

32
00:02:25.316 --> 00:02:29.001
If I take them off, I look weird! See?

33
00:02:29.002 --> 00:02:31.307
I don't even look like me!"

34
00:02:31.308 --> 00:02:33.463
Laura closed her suitcase.

35
00:02:33.464 --> 00:02:37.826
"Thank you," she said and returned to her desk.

36
00:02:37.827 --> 00:02:41.440
"That was great!" Joy told her.

37
00:02:41.441 --> 00:02:43.810
Next was Joy's presentation.

38
00:02:43.811 --> 00:02:47.835
"I'm going to talk about how to build friendships.

39
00:02:47.836 --> 00:02:52.891
First, I want you all to be friendly listeners during my report.

40
00:02:52.892 --> 00:02:57.248
Please turn your bodies toward me and look into my eyes."

41
00:02:57.249 --> 00:03:00.172
Joy looked around the room.

42
00:03:00.173 --> 00:03:05.098
"Good. Now, while I'm talking, don't let your mind wander off.

43
00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:08.165
Pay attention!" She smiled.

44
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:11.760
"Is everybody ready to be a friendly listener?"

45
00:03:11.761 --> 00:03:14.401
Everyone nodded at Joy.

46
00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:20.235
"If you see someone who looks like a nice person, say something friendly.

47
00:03:20.236 --> 00:03:23.560
That's how to start a new friendship.

48
00:03:23.561 --> 00:03:27.563
You could offer to help carry groceries or books.

49
00:03:27.564 --> 00:03:29.442
The opposite works too!

50
00:03:29.443 --> 00:03:31.931
Ask someone to help you!"

51
00:03:31.932 --> 00:03:37.784
Katie nodded. She remembered how Olivia had asked for help at the library.

52
00:03:37.785 --> 00:03:41.616
She turned and smiled at her new friend.

53
00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:47.781
"You can also say someone has a nice haircut or cute sneakers," said Joy.

54
00:03:47.782 --> 00:03:53.813
"On the first day of school, Laura told Olivia that her kukui nut necklace was cool.

55
00:03:53.814 --> 00:03:56.054
That was a friendly thing to say."

56
00:03:56.055 --> 00:04:01.346
Joy took a breath, smiled at Laura, and continued.

57
00:04:01.347 --> 00:04:05.636
"Here are some other ways to be a good friend," she said.

58
00:04:05.637 --> 00:04:09.210
"Be kind. Don't make fun of your friends."

59
00:04:09.211 --> 00:04:13.033
"Does that mean don't tease?" asked Katie.

60
00:04:13.034 --> 00:04:15.479
She looked at Luke.

61
00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.266
"Make sure your friends can count on you.

62
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:21.738
Don't back out on promises or plans."

63
00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:25.171
Luke and Carlos looked at Katie.

64
00:04:25.172 --> 00:04:30.793
"Don't be bossy," said Joy.

65
00:04:30.794 --> 00:04:34.712
"Why is everyone looking at me?" cried Katie.

66
00:04:34.713 --> 00:04:38.557
"Let's be good listeners," said Ms. Barrow.

67
00:04:38.558 --> 00:04:41.918
"That means no interrupting."

68
00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.061
"Now this is important," Joy went on.

69
00:04:46.062 --> 00:04:51.203
"If you fight with your friends, make up as soon as you can.

70
00:04:51.204 --> 00:04:54.634
Say, 'I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said that.'

71
00:04:54.635 --> 00:04:57.850
Or say, 'I made a mistake.'"

72
00:04:57.851 --> 00:05:01.261
Joy reached into a paper bag.

73
00:05:01.262 --> 00:05:05.132
"This is my friendship meter," she said.

74
00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:10.661
"Right now some friends in this room are making the friendship meter unhappy."

75
00:05:10.662 --> 00:05:15.779
Joy looked at Luke, then Carlos, then Katie.

76
00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.159
"The friends have had a fight," she said.

77
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.569
"But I think it's time to make up!"
